        "id": 1599263
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T11:57:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Different types of storage devices in ChromeOS might affect how fast it can write data. Even for the same eMMC device, its performance depends on its run-time usage. For example, when an eMMC device reaches 90% capacity, it takes 3x longer to write compared to when it was at 30% capacity.\n\nSo, using sysprop to manage this wait time offers several advantages:\n\n1. Centralized Management: Platform-specific configurations are easier to maintain in a central local. Especially when number for platforms and parameters increases.\n\n2. Consistent Approach: This aligns with how other configurations (connection, scan parameters) are handled.\n\n3. Model-Based Customization: Different ChromeOS boards can have tailored configurations.",
      "parentUuid": "e3492222_61b1f3b2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "b4191ba199c1255bfddc6a352344a10e211278bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e3b53ec_dd934c3a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
